WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.801
-Our next guest is
an Academy Award-nominated

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.300
and Emmy Award-winning producer

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.434
His latest work,
"The Exorcist: Believer,"

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.868
is out now, and his other movie,
"Friday Nights at Freddy's,"

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:12.767
comes to theaters and streaming
on Peacock October 27th.

00:00:12.767 --> 00:00:13.934
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.000
[Buzzes]

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.334
-You must be
the new security guard.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.767
-Back in the '80s,
some kids went missing.

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.801
That's why the place shut down.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.300
What is she doing here?

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.534
-I couldn't find a sitter.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:26.934
What are you so afraid of?

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.634
-Them.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.167
[ Screams ]

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.601
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.801
our good friend Jason Blum,
everybody!

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:43.501
♪♪

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:49.534
♪♪

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:52.367
Welcome back, my friend.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.100
-Thrilled to be here.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.367
"Five Nights at Freddy's"
-Five. What did I say?

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.334
-"Friday Nights at Freddy's."
-I said Friday.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:00:59.567
It's "Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:01.300
-Everyone says
"Friday Nights at Freddy's."

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.467
-Why do we get it wrong?

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:03.767
-"Five Nights at Freddy's."
I don't know.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:05.834
The sequel is going to be
"Friday Nights at Freddy's."

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.434
The guy who created
it just had a heart attack.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.367
-Oh, my God.
"Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.400
Alright. That's very --

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.167
And this
is based on a video game.

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:15.934
-This is based on a video game
and very, very complicated lore,

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:18.834
and I've been working on it --
I've worked on this movie

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:21.033
longer than anything else
we've ever done.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:23.334
I've worked on it,
it's been 8 or 9 years

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.200
since I first met Scott Cawthon,
who created this,

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.200
and he's
a wildly creative genius

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.701
and he lives in Texas.

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:35.567
And it was very, very important
to him that it be just so.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:38.667
We went through
8 directors and 15 scripts,

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:42.067
and I'm very, very proud
we finally got the movie.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.834
-And then I'm out here
just getting the title wrong.

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:48.334
-Yeah, and then you destroyed it
in a heartbeat.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.467
-12 years of your life!

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.000
-12 years of my life, ruined.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.968
Now, we did something
interesting on the movie.

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:57.167
Usually, when Hollywood
attacks a video game or a book,

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.801
they always say, like,
"We're going to make it

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:01.033
for the fans and we're going to
make it for everybody else."

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.934
I probably shouldn't be saying
this on national television,

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.567
but I'm just going to go for it.
-That's alright. It's on late.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:06.834
-Yeah, yeah. True, true. Not
that many people. Okay, fine.

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:10.667
So what what
what Scott wanted to do,

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.400
which is an experiment,
we'll see how it works.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.701
I thought it was a very
cool idea, so we said yes,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:18.534
is we are only
making this for fans

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:19.868
of "Five Nights at Freddy's."

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.767
If other people want to see it,
that's fine with us.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.000
We're very happy.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.100
But we're not trying
to expand the audience.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.701
We're trying to keep
the fans thrilled.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.868
And of course,
we won't make everyone happy,

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:32.133
but that's what we did

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.701
setting out to make the movie,
which is unusual.

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.734
And as I said,
the PR team probably now

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:39.267
is going to come assassinate me,
but that's what we did.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:42.133
-And do you feel that there is
a groundswell of excitement

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.968
from the fans, knowing
that this is the approach?

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:46.367
-Yes, the movie is right now --

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.734
I have a little grin on my face,

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.567
because the movie
is looking like --

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.868
you never know with these
things, as I recently learned,

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:56.667
but it's looking like it
is going to way overperform

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.901
what anyone, including myself,
thought it would do.

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:00.400
So knock on wood, that happens.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.701
-Knock on wood. Very exciting.
-So far, so good.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.934
-You are
a horror movie producer.

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:07.200
This should come as no surprise,
you love Halloween.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.567
-I'm a Halloween expert.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:10.534
-Favorite holiday?
-I'm like Santa for Halloween.

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:11.701
-You are like Santa
for Halloween.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:12.968
Yes, I've been
at Halloween parties.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.434
You show up, never,
not once without a costume.

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.834
-I don't mess around.

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:19.200
-But you also have access
to very good makeup people,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.634
very good costumes.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.100
-No, it's true, I cheat a bit.
-You cheat a bit.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.300
Like, for example,
you and your wife,

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.601
your beautiful wife Lauren --

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:28.634
decided to be Stormy Daniels
and Michael Avenatti

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:30.200
a few years ago.
-Yes, we did.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.467
-But you went
a different way with it.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.601
-Yes, we did.
We flipped genders.

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:34.734
-You flipped genders.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.601
-Not bad.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.000
-Come on!

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.234
-That's you.
-That was incredible.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:42.467
-That's incredible.

00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:43.834
-People look at -- when
I show that to people,

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.467
they really, they look.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:46.767
It takes like, four seconds

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.334
to understand
what's actually happening.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:50.767
-Yeah.
-But this is actually me,

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.567
and this is actually my wife.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.501
-And how uncomfortable
was that evening?

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:55.434
-It was --

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.667
It was actually physically,

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.133
profoundly uncomfortable
because I had

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:00.467
10 pounds of prosthetics on me.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.667
Is that what you mean?
-Yeah.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.133
-It was very and very
uncomfortable and sweaty,

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:05.267
and I feel terrible for women
in these clothes

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:06.601
that they have to wear, it's
horrible, and in high heels.

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:08.400
-Did not stop you guys

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.601
from doing Jared and Ivanka,
though.

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:10.534
-Jared and Ivanka.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.934
-Yeah.
-That was a great one.

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:14.868
Remember when Jared put on
that crazy vest,

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:17.501
you thought he was fighting
the war in Afghanistan?

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.067
This was great.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:20.667
-You produced, "M3GAN,"
a fantastic film.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:21.767
-Yes, a great film.
-And you decided --

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.000
[ Applause ]

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.667
-There we go. Give it up.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:28.100
-You -- The red carpet had
multiple M3GANs.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.467
I don't want to give it away
for the audience.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:32.033
-Yes, go ahead.
-There's five M3GANS

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:33.234
in this photo.
-Yes, yes.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.734
-Jason is one of the M3GANs.
-This is tricky.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.801 --> 00:04:42.501
-This might be best of all.

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:44.000
You did
Wicked Witch of the West.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.467
And I mean, this is fantastic.

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:47.934
Look at you.
-You know.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:49.801
-And then finally,
you let Lauren

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:51.701
be appropriate as Dorothy there.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:53.767
I look like a witch
in real life, so it worked.

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:57.267
-Now, you had a very
interesting producer problem

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:59.267
that you ran into,
because I don't think people

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:02.300
appreciate how important a date
is to when a movie comes out.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.801
So you have this movie,
"The Exorcist,"

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.467
you have a date picked out,
a date you're excited about.

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:07.734
-Yes.

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:10.701
-And usually, you know
which movies are coming.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.267
Movies never come
out of nowhere.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:13.400
-No.
-And then one did.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.701
-And then one did.

00:05:14.701 --> 00:05:17.467
-This was a terrible tragedy
in the Blum household.

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:21.634
Friday the 13th in October
is the single greatest day

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.601
to release a horror movie,
and it only comes around

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.334
once every seven years
because there aren't that many.

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:27.033
Friday the 13ths in October,

00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:28.834
they're just the once
every seven years.

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:33.100
So we date "The Exorcist" on the
greatest date for horror movies,

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.834
that comes around
very infrequently

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:40.467
and about eight weeks ago,

00:05:40.467 --> 00:05:44.133
which is the last possible
minute you can change a date,

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:48.434
Taylor Swift drops on my date.

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:51.634
I try and save the day
by "ExorSwift."

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:54.434
I try and make --
I'm hoping, praying,

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:55.767
that this is going to work.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:58.267
-When you say you tried to make
"ExorSwift" a thing,

00:05:58.267 --> 00:05:59.868
here's his efforts, by the way.

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.033
-"Exorswift."

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:02.934
Yeah, well,
I didn't try that hard.

00:06:02.934 --> 00:06:06.934
I didn't try that hard.
I tried, I tried.

00:06:06.934 --> 00:06:07.968
Three hours,

00:06:07.968 --> 00:06:10.334
three hours after
after I tweet that,

00:06:10.334 --> 00:06:12.234
the head of the marketing,

00:06:12.234 --> 00:06:14.634
amazing partner Michael Moses,
calls me and says,

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.868
"It's not working.
We got to move the movie."

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:18.334
-And so, and then,
this is the follow-up tweet

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:19.467
just a little bit --

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:20.501
"Look what you made me do.

00:06:20.501 --> 00:06:22.200
"The Exorcist: Believer"
moves to 10/6.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.234
#TaylorWins.

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:25.667
-Taylor wins.

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:27.067
Yeah, I was trying
to be a nice guy,

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:28.834
because Taylor Swift is
my daughter's favorite singer,

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:34.267
but underneath this tweet there
was rage, rage, rage.

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:36.234
-And it affected
the whole Blum household,

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:37.801
because your wife, Lauren Blum,

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.434
who's a fantastic
screenwriter --

00:06:39.434 --> 00:06:40.534
-Incredible.

00:06:40.534 --> 00:06:42.400
-Her and her partner,
Rebecca Angelo,

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.267
wrote a fantastic film
called "Dumb Money."

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:46.868
-Yes, exactly.
-"Dumb Money."

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:48.667
[ Applause ]

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:51.000
And "Dumb Money" is up
against a problem

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.767
a lot of these
smaller movies are having.

00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:55.567
SAG actors cannot promote
the film.

00:06:55.567 --> 00:06:57.434
But she had
to move her date as well.

00:06:57.434 --> 00:06:59.567
-Well, so what happened is,

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:01.334
we had to move the movie back,

00:07:01.334 --> 00:07:04.901
and it just so happened that
"Dumb Money" was on that date.

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:09.334
So not only did Taylor Swift
destroy my Friday the 13th

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:13.400
and kill this
incredible date I had,

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.100
she almost caused me
to get divorced.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.400
-Because you moved
back to 10/6...

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.567
-We put on "Dumb Money,"
and my wife said

00:07:19.567 --> 00:07:21.033
"You can move anywhere else,
but not there."

00:07:21.033 --> 00:07:23.300
I said,
"There's nowhere else to go."

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:28.200
And it was a very tense
24 hours, until my poor wife

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:31.968
had to move her
spectacular movie earlier.

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:33.667
But it's very hard,
these movies,

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:35.934
especially in today's
environment, it's very fragile

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:38.334
and it's very delicate
and moving release dates

00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:40.267
is not something you want to do.

00:07:40.267 --> 00:07:41.601
So what can I do?

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:44.634
My daughter loves Taylor Swift,
so I feel bad, you know?

00:07:44.634 --> 00:07:47.133
And everyone loves Taylor Swift,
so if I said anything bad --

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:48.834
-Taylor Swift
is going to be fine.

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:51.234
-Taylor Swift
loves Taylor Swift.

00:07:51.234 --> 00:07:52.801
-I love Taylor Swift!

00:07:52.801 --> 00:07:54.567
-I can't get Taylor Swift?

00:07:54.567 --> 00:07:56.601
I can't affect her by talking
about her on this show?

00:07:56.601 --> 00:07:58.801
-No, I think her movie
is going to do just fine.

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:01.467
-No, that's the problem.
It's going to do amazing.

00:08:01.467 --> 00:08:04.434
It's going to do amazing,
and we had to move.

00:08:04.434 --> 00:08:05.868
We had to move all our movies.
We almost got divorced.

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:07.968
-Did you think about maybe in
the middle of "The Exorcist"

00:08:07.968 --> 00:08:10.934
just adding a scene
of like, Taylor Swift singing?

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:12.067
-I did. Actually, I did.

00:08:12.067 --> 00:08:13.601
I said,
"We could either move the date,

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:17.133
we could just add some of
her footage into the movie."

00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:19.067
-You got one of your dreams
coming true.

00:08:19.067 --> 00:08:20.667
You are going to be
a judge on Shark Tank.

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:23.200
-Oh, yes. This is very
exciting to talk about.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:26.067
[ Applause ]
-Yeah, tell me more.

00:08:26.067 --> 00:08:28.234
-I get asked by people.

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:31.267
This is actually, I'll connect
to your show for a sec.

00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:32.400
I get asked by people,

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.968
"So did they ask you
to do 'Shark Tank'?"

00:08:33.968 --> 00:08:35.834
I don't know about all these
other successful people.

00:08:35.834 --> 00:08:37.033
I've never been asked to do --

00:08:37.033 --> 00:08:39.167
I begged to be on "Shark Tank"
for 20 years,

00:08:39.167 --> 00:08:41.367
just like I begged to be
on your show for 20 years.

00:08:41.367 --> 00:08:42.634
I mean, very similar.
-Yeah.

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:45.534
-Anyway, they finally said yes,
and it was great.

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:48.501
And then of course, I get on
"Shark Tank" and I'm doing...

00:08:48.501 --> 00:08:51.601
Now everyone says, "So what are
you selling on 'Shark Tank'?"

00:08:51.601 --> 00:08:53.534
I'm like, "I'm a Shark,
for God's sake!

00:08:53.534 --> 00:08:55.868
I'm not [bleep].
I'm not selling."

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:59.667
They think I'm selling
Blumhouse on "Shark Tank."

00:08:59.667 --> 00:09:03.334
For $1 million,
you can have 10% of Blumhouse.

00:09:03.334 --> 00:09:05.767
So anyway, I was a shark
on "Shark Tank."

00:09:05.767 --> 00:09:07.868
I did it, they taped
two episodes for the day.

00:09:07.868 --> 00:09:10.234
You go at 8:00 and you leave
at 8:00 at night or whatever.

00:09:10.234 --> 00:09:13.033
It was really fun.
It was really exciting.

00:09:13.033 --> 00:09:16.367
And I had a great day. And it
airs -- it airs very soon.

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:19.033
I should know the date when I'm
supposed to be plugging it --

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:20.400
-All you know are
the dates of your movies.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.934
-All I know is the dates
of Taylor Swift, "ExorSwift."

00:09:22.934 --> 00:09:24.901
-#ExorSwift.

00:09:24.901 --> 00:09:26.334
-It comes out at the end
of this month.

00:09:26.334 --> 00:09:28.834
-And were there,
just as a little teaser,

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:30.267
were there anything
you were impressed by?

00:09:30.267 --> 00:09:32.067
-There were some things I was --

00:09:32.067 --> 00:09:34.100
I've been instructed very --

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.667
You can't say
if you invested or not,

00:09:35.667 --> 00:09:38.167
so you'll have to watch
the show to find out.

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:40.601
But there were several things
